# Vial size and label profile

Discuss and reason about **vial size** (e.g. **3 ml**, **10 ml**) as the product concept; **label dimensions and preview scaling** follow from the active **vial profile**.

## Vial profiles (product intent)

Implemented and planned vial sizes are described in [docs/FRD.md](../../docs/FRD.md) (**Today** / **Planned**). Only **3 ml** is wired in code today.

| Vial size | Code source of truth | Notes |
|-----------|----------------------|--------|
| **3 ml** | `src/features/label/LabelConfig.ts` (`LABEL_CONFIG`) | Dimensions (currently **40 × 20 mm**), padding, **203 DPI** printer assumption, `baseContainerWidthPx` for preview scaling. |
| **10 ml** | Not implemented | See FRD **Planned**; extend config (profiles/presets) when built. |

When the user has not named a vial size, follow **`label-work-clarify-vial-size.mdc`** before changing label-related behavior.

## Mental model

- Output targets **small adhesive stock** at **203 DPI-class thermal** (e.g. Niimbot): binary dots, bleed/bloom — **legibility on paper** beats “looks fine zoomed on a monitor.”
- **`LABEL_CONFIG`** is canonical for whichever profile is active; changing mm/DPI/preview base requires updating layout (`LabelLayoutEngine`, `LabelComposer`, `Scaling`), tests, and preview/export together.
- PNG/export constraints: **`thermal-print-output.mdc`**.

Prefer checking **export/preview at realistic zoom** for the **target vial profile**, not full-screen dev chrome.
